1
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,280
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,840
and for entertainment purposes only.
Viewer discretion is advised

3
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,960
It's me, Nakhun…

4
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:25,960
<i>My mission: Find out whatever happened</i>
<i>to the real Klao.</i>

5
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,920
<i>Is there a matter</i>
<i>you wish to discuss?</i>

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,520
-I want to visit the capital.
-Have you sought his permission, Master?

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,439
Yes.

8
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,760
-Help! Help me!
-Be wary, my Lady!

9
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,400
<i>Help me!</i>

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,040
<i>-Help! Help me!</i>
<i>-Be wary, my Lady!</i>

11
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,560
Help me! I can bear it no more!

12
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,520
Help! I can bear it no longer!

13
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,960
-Cease this harassment, Cherd.
-Mind your own affairs!

14
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,160
This matter is none of your concern!

15
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,280
Meddle not, or you shall face my wrath!

16
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,800
-Be wary, my Lady.
-Trying to slip away?

17
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:59,160
You dare escape my reach?

18
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,200
-My Lady!
-My Lady!

19
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,239
Who dares?

20
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,000
Klao…

21
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,720
You… You…

22
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,560
You know me?

23
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,080
You… You…

24
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,400
What?

25
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,360
What of me?

26
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,040
Master Klao.

27
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:29,400
Let us return.

28
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,480
Who's this dude? What's his name?

29
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,000
It is best not to meddle with him, Master.

30
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,480
Have I truly been forgotten by you?

31
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,600
Yeah.

32
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,280
What is the meaning of this commotion?

33
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,880
Harn…

34
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,160
My Lord…

35
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,520
Varna…

36
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,440
What has unfolded here?

37
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,120
My purse of coins slipped from my grasp.

38
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,520
This man managed to retrieve it.

39
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,320
Rather than return it graciously,

40
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,480
he chose to flirt

41
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,840
and seize my wrist.

42
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:09,880
However, this man

43
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:12,520
came to my rescue.

44
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,680
You have my deepest gratitude.

45
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:18,920
Dear Klao.

46
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,960
The common folk said that

47
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,760
you had gone missing.

48
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,200
Have you at last returned?

49
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:33,160
<i>He knows me too?</i>

50
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,120
Dear Klao.

51
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,840
By what means have you returned?

52
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,400
Where did you disappear to?

53
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,240
I…

54
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,600
I…

55
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,560
Think no more of it.

56
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,200
As for you, Cherd,

57
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,120
you shall suffer for your insolence
and lawlessness.

58
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,600
My Lord, I…

59
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,080
I did but jest with the lady.

60
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,720
There was no malice in my heart.

61
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:19,560
I knew not that she was your lady.

62
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:24,000
Varna is the daughter of my own uncle.

63
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,400
She arrived from the city of Lavo
but yesterday!

64
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,960
-Correct your understanding at once.
-Yes, my Lord.

65
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,200
Away with them, you two.

66
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,440
Their punishment shall await my arrival.

67
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,280
Varna, return to the manor at once.

68
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,160
The capital is vast and sprawling,
unlike the city of Lavo.

69
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:50,400
The darker it gets,
the more dangerous.

70
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,520
Yes, my Lord.

71
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,160
Yes, my Lord…

72
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,760
And you as well.

73
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:00,920
Klao!

74
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,200
<i>Twin Phops…</i>

75
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,680
<i>They're gonna tear me to shreds.</i>

76
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,720
<i>Who let you enter the scene</i>
<i>at this moment?</i>

77
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,800
We promised to be here together.

78
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:08,040
Why did you come by yourself?

79
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,240
I came here with Chuay.

80
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,080
I didn't come here by myself.

81
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,720
Yes, my Lord.

82
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,760
I have kept a close eye upon Master Klao.

83
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,440
He has always been with me.

84
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:24,280
He has not given himself over
to debauchery.

85
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,320
Halt.

86
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,280
I have yet to utter a word of reproach.

87
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,520
My Lord.

88
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,720
I am Varna,

89
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:37,680
the daughter
of High Lord Dech Kraisor of Lavo.

90
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,320
Do you recognize me,
the lady standing before you, my Lord?

91
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,800
I do.

92
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:45,840
You are of the Lord's kin.

93
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,080
We met during the previous year,

94
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,720
while I was traveling with my father
on royal service.

95
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,160
Have you two been acquainted?

96
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:03,240
Only a few days have passed
since I came to this city, my Lord.

97
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,520
My father strictly enjoined me

98
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:09,080
to render my most humble respects
at the feet of High Lord Pichayabhakdi.

99
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,960
I intend to depart tomorrow.

100
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,840
I had not anticipated that
our paths would cross so soon.

101
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,960
<i>Righto, Mr. Sexy Boy of Ayutthaya.</i>

102
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,840
<i>Everyone is swooning over you.</i>

103
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,080
Chuay.

104
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,440
Escort your master to the pier.

105
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,240
Yes, my Lord.

106
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,120
Phop.

107
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:45,440
We made a promise, didn't we?

108
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:47,240
Do go.

109
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,600
I have matters to discuss with the Lord.

110
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,480
Master, let us leave.

111
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,640
I'm not leaving.

112
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,400
Master Klao!

113
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,280
Master!

114
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,240
This way, Master.

115
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,040
I beg of you, Master, follow me.

116
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,600
Gosh.

117
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,640
Deary me, Master.

118
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:18,000
I have already cautioned you
that we ought to wait for the Lord.

119
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,640
It's fine.

120
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,520
In the end, we met him here.

121
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,800
Master!

122
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:24,320
This is no jest.

123
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,720
Did I not warn you? Trouble has arisen

124
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:28,160
of our meeting with Cherd.

125
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,920
What is there to worry about?

126
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,200
Who is he?

127
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:34,880
Why can't I meet him?

128
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,080
Did Klao have a beef with Cherd
in the past?

129
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:44,920
What happened?

130
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:50,760
Were we friends?

131
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,880
Did I owe him money?

132
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,360
Did we date the same person?

133
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,680
By dating, I mean…

134
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,880
Falling in love.

135
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,920
If not dating…

136
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,720
Someone in the talking stage?

137
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,280
A man?

138
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,040
Or… was it a woman?

139
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:33,360
That troublemaker and Klao
once fought over a woman, huh?

140
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,560
Who was she?

141
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,040
I know nothing of it, Master.

142
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,840
I can speak no more.

143
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,600
Guess I have to look into it myself?

144
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,320
Gosh.

145
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,600
And…

146
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,520
Phop told us to wait here, right?

147
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,960
How upsetting!

148
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,840
So that is how the matter stands.

149
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:24,640
Pray accept my apologies
for the disturbance he caused,

150
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,920
and my thanks
for overseeing the commotion,

151
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,640
especially as it lies
beyond your usual jurisdiction.

152
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,280
It is of no account.

153
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,600
Pray think nothing of it.

154
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,360
I am beholden to him

155
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,000
for coming to her aid.

156
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:45,960
Lord.

157
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,400
Forgive my intrusion…

158
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,800
but I find

159
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,320
Dear Klao's demeanor most peculiar.

160
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:02,040
Despite his enmity toward Cherd,

161
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,920
he regards them
as if they were but strangers.

162
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,000
He treats even me with the same reserve.

163
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:10,320
What has taken hold of him?

164
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:16,040
Surely, the intent was
but to provoke his temper.

165
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,760
But does that apply to me as well?

166
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:26,040
Dear Klao's resentment toward him
must be so profound

167
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,400
that he has turned his anger upon you.

168
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,320
Allow me to make amends for his conduct.

169
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,160
Any soul would pity Dear Klao,

170
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:49,720
for Lord Preechapiban's judicial matter
was a crushing ordeal.

171
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,440
It is more than any son should bear,

172
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:57,520
especially one
in so precarious a state of mind.

173
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,040
I can well understand it.

174
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,160
This is taking too long.

175
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:19,200
What could those Twin Phops
possibly be chatting about?

176
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:22,440
It's so hot out here.

177
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,960
I want a bottle of Ichitan so bad!

178
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:36,080
ICHITAN HONEY LEMON GREEN TEA

179
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,360
"I…"

180
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,080
I beg your pardon, Master?

181
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:46,120
You don't know what Ichitan is?

182
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,000
Right.

183
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,000
It's tea.

184
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:54,920
Green tea.

185
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,120
It's refreshing
and keeps us on top of our game.

186
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
"On top of the game?"

187
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,600
It makes us feel full of beans.

188
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,520
Full of…

189
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,640
Beans?

190
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,840
What was that you said?

191
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,440
Forget it.

192
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,680
By the way,

193
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,320
do people in Ayutthaya

194
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,240
drink tea?

195
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,400
Are there any cafes

196
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,800
or tea shops here?

197
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,680
There is indeed a teahouse, Master.

198
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,000
It is Meng's.

199
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:32,400
But they do not serve a tea full of beans.

200
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,920
There is one?

201
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,840
Cool!

202
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,960
Let's go to the teahouse. Come on!

203
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,720
Oh, Master.

204
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,440
I shall remain here.

205
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,280
I'd never dare defy the Lord again.

206
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:46,040
Heaven knows how many cane strokes
await me for escorting you here in secret.

207
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,880
Until the lesson is well learned…

208
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,560
so you never take him
on such diversions again.

209
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:01,520
Phop, don't blame him for this.

210
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:06,280
I was the one
who talked him into bringing me here.

211
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:09,240
Have you learned to take responsibility
for your actions?

212
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:12,080
Punish me all you want,

213
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:15,080
but please bring me to a cafe.

214
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,320
I mean, the teahouse.

215
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,240
I'm so, so thirsty,

216
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:25,800
I might even drink canal water
just to quench it.

217
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:34,160
Do not attempt to sway me
with such sly looks.

218
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,640
Chuay.

219
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,480
Remain here.

220
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,080
Come with me.

221
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,720
Remember this.

222
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,040
You are to go nowhere
unless it be with me, and me alone.

223
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,560
This way.

224
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,680
Right this way.

225
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:19,360
Oh, my Lord.

226
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,600
Pray, step inside, my Lord.

227
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,720
"My Lord?"

228
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:32,920
Which lord do you mean, A-Chai?

229
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:36,760
There are so many lords in this land.

230
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,240
Which one do you mean?

231
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,600
Deary me…

232
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,040
I wonder which lord it is--

233
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,160
Lord Phop, is it not?

234
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,880
There is nothing illicit
in this establishment, my Lord.

235
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:51,560
There are…
There are no thieves here.

236
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,360
There are no outlaws
or thieves inside, my Lord.

237
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,480
I have not come to hunt down thieves,

238
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,760
only to bring my brother for a cup of tea.

239
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,720
What a relief…

240
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,880
I bid welcome to Lord Phop's brother--

241
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,200
Good heavens!

242
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:07,120
Klao!

243
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,880
Klao…

244
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:12,000
Our teahouse does not offer spirits.

245
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,760
It has been ages since we last did so.

246
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,160
Klao…

247
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,960
Take it easy, Master.

248
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:23,000
You look rather bright and lively,

249
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:25,520
neither intoxicated nor aggressive.

250
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,480
Welcome to the teahouse.

251
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:30,200
We have a tea
we would like you to try.

252
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:33,000
-Come inside for freshly brewed tea.
-Pray, step inside.

253
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:37,040
Is he going
to reduce my chairs to splinters?

254
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,200
<i>Klao got so drunk that he caused trouble?</i>

255
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:49,040
It is ready.

256
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:52,680
Da Hong Pao.

257
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,120
This is the tea.

258
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,920
Drinking it shall compel you
to utter the word,

259
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,840
"Delicious!"

260
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,680
It is very delightful.

261
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,840
It is the very tea favored

262
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:06,000
by the current emperor himself.

263
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,960
This comes from Fujian.

264
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,319
Fujian?

265
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,240
It is a province

266
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:16,800
whose capital is Fuzhou.

267
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:20,480
This particular tea shall rejuvenate

268
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,880
your soul,

269
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:24,599
as if a bodhisattva's chant

270
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,280
were echoing within your heart.

271
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,720
Master.

272
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:46,760
What was that?

273
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,880
It was the chant of a bodhisattva.

274
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:52,000
I merely wished to provide you
with a clearer perspective.

275
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,360
It is as simple as that.

276
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,880
Steamed pork buns

277
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:58,840
-and freshly made <i>mantou</i> are here.
-Here.

278
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,800
My goodness!
To enjoy these together with tea…

279
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,200
Da…

280
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:09,000
-Hong Pao?
-Wonderful. Your memory is just as sharp.

281
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:10,760
Too much drinking dulls your mind.

282
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,400
-It is my duty--
-Master?

283
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,800
Customers.

284
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,160
Foreigners are here.

285
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:19,840
Kindly enjoy the steamed buns
and Da Hong Pao while I am away.

286
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:23,120
Oh, welcome.

287
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,280
If Master gets to talk to Muan,

288
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,960
I bet it'd be a really fun time.

289
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:33,200
In that case,
who shall be their listener?

290
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,360
Mark.

291
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:56,840
<i>-That's Nakhun Phattanatada for you…</i>
-My! You can speak their tongue?

292
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,920
<i>…the top student in Shakespeare Studies.</i>

293
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,400
Wonderful, wonderful.

294
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:13,360
What color is the banana
called in the Farangi tongue?

295
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,600
What about that fruit?

296
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,240
-What about that dessert?
-<i>Khanom tako!</i>

297
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,920
Not funny?

298
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,640
Your way of speaking Thai
is quite peculiar.

299
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:34,800
How do you speak the foreign tongue
so fluently?

300
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,720
Where did you acquire such skill?

301
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,160
Was it in Phichit as well?

302
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:46,160
I learned it in Phichit, my Lord.

303
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,640
<i>I shouldn't have said that.</i>

304
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:56,320
<i>He has even more reason</i>
<i>to be suspicious now.</i>

305
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,720
The Farangi soldiers
we just encountered…

306
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:02,600
I once mediated a dispute
between one of them and a vendor.

307
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:05,320
However, with no one
to bridge the language gap,

308
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:09,080
both sides departed
equally dissatisfied and misunderstood.

309
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:13,720
In due time,
you shall teach me this foreign tongue.

310
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,800
Were I literate in the language,

311
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,360
I could do so much more for our people.

312
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:27,960
Master Klao.

313
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:31,760
How was your time
at the teahouse, Master Klao?

314
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:33,080
You look rather delighted.

315
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,160
Trouble upon trouble.

316
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:37,720
Do not venture out on your own again.

317
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,800
Isn't it clear how peril lurks everywhere?

318
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,520
What peril?

319
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,600
My time in Phichit
was even more dangerous.

320
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,960
I saw giant crocodiles.

321
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,280
Have you ever heard of Chalawan?

322
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:49,800
Master Klao.

323
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,560
Who is Charles Le Wand?

324
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:53,360
Gosh…

325
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,720
That is not the kind of danger
I was referring to.

326
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:58,280
I was speaking of the ruffians.

327
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:01,640
Perhaps you are unaware that

328
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:04,520
you have more adversaries
than you can fathom.

329
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:06,600
But

330
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:10,120
this is bringing back
so many of my memories.

331
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,160
Even so, the risk outweighs
any possible gain.

332
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:17,400
It is well that
Lord Harn intervened in time.

333
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:20,120
Without him, you could've ended up
fighting Cherd again.

334
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,080
I am not quarreling with you.

335
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:31,200
I am concerned for your safety.

336
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:35,120
I already know that.

337
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,760
That said, step into the boat.

338
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,440
Let us set sail.

339
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:07,360
Yes, my Lord.

340
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:13,720
Fortune teller? Wait, it's her!

341
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,720
Be wary, Master Klao.

342
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:19,200
Chuay, leave without me.
Let me go talk to her.

343
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:22,200
Where is this fortune teller?

344
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:24,400
-I have yet to see a single soul.
-She's…

345
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,400
But I…

346
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,280
Jom…

347
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:00,320
What is it that catches your eye?

348
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,800
Is there something upon my face?

349
00:25:08,280 --> 00:25:10,520
No, not at all…

350
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:13,200
Are you making herbal remedies?

351
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:14,160
Yes, of course.

352
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:17,680
Did you take this for washing clothes?

353
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:20,240
Have you gone mad, like Klao has?

354
00:25:21,280 --> 00:25:23,600
I was but making conversation.

355
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:28,440
Have there been many patients today?

356
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:30,360
Are you exhausted, Jom?

357
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:33,480
To what end
do you repeat these same questions?

358
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:37,720
No reason, really.
I have brought you some food.

359
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:41,240
I feared you might go without food again.

360
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:44,360
Always tending to my needs…

361
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:47,720
Have you no other duties to attend to?

362
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:52,320
I finished all my household chores
this morning.

363
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:58,960
Kaew.

364
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:03,240
You are a man.
You should be out there, making your way

365
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:06,040
for the sake of those at home.

366
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:12,280
There is so much to be done here,

367
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:14,440
and we are short-handed.

368
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:16,640
You are the son of a high lord.

369
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,400
Be strong and courageous,

370
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:21,600
so that you may protect your family.

371
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,880
Now then, will you give me my meal,

372
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:59,480
or must I drink your tears instead?

373
00:27:05,840 --> 00:27:07,520
So you will eat then?

374
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,160
Put it on a plate for me.

375
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:15,920
If there is no work to be done,

376
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,040
then help me
fashion these herbal remedies.

377
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:54,800
<i>Cherd? My enemy? We fought over a girl?</i>

378
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:00,080
Help me!

379
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:01,040
Klao!

380
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,600
<i>Or is there something else?</i>

381
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:22,080
Clinging to your master's side?
Soon enough, your wife might be gone.

382
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:23,520
Watch over her for me then.

383
00:28:23,600 --> 00:28:25,280
I am too concerned about my master.

384
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:26,960
Your master is no longer a child.

385
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,960
Why must you watch over him so intently?

386
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,960
Then why are you loitering here,
staring me down?

387
00:28:38,040 --> 00:28:43,360
<i>Lord Harn is Phop's colleague,</i>
<i>or is there something more?</i>

388
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:46,160
You look rather bright and lively,

389
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:48,720
neither intoxicated nor aggressive.

390
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:58,360
<i>Meng knew that Klao was an alcoholic.</i>

391
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:05,960
<i>An outburst at the teahouse?</i>

392
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:09,280
<i>Was it related to Cherd or something?</i>

393
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,360
Is he refusing to eat?

394
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:24,800
My knuckles are sore
from all the knocking,

395
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,720
yet he refuses to come out, my Lord.

396
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:44,520
<i>And what's the deal</i>
<i>with the fortune teller?</i>

397
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:45,880
<i>Is she just a look-alike?</i>

398
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,640
<i>Or…</i>

399
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:53,280
Do you believe in multiple lifetimes?

400
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:56,720
<i>Reincarnation?</i>

401
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:04,040
<i>No! That's insane. That's impossible.</i>

402
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:12,240
<i>Traveling through time myself</i>

403
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,120
<i>also sounds impossible.</i>

404
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:20,040
<i>Be careful, Nakhun.</i>

405
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:23,720
In the world of time travel literature,

406
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:27,680
we cannot always rely on logic.

407
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:31,880
<i>It might reflect something</i>

408
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:34,160
that lies deep within.

409
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:00,160
How the hell did she get here?

410
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:05,000
Fortune teller?

411
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,000
It really is you, isn't it?

412
00:31:07,080 --> 00:31:08,440
No.

413
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:10,720
I tell no fortunes.

414
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:13,680
Come on. Stop playing around.

415
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:17,280
Hey.

416
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:19,240
It's just the two of us now.

417
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,680
No need to hide your true self.

418
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:24,800
Did you also travel through time with me,

419
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:29,880
or did you reincarnate
as Fortune Teller Rattikarn?

420
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,880
Hey.

421
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:32,920
Answer me.

422
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:35,800
Rattikarn!

423
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:38,120
Dark and cold!

424
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:40,920
Such agony.

425
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:44,600
Can you not speak in riddles?
Say something easy to understand.

426
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:46,640
Help.

427
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:53,520
Can't breathe!

428
00:31:54,840 --> 00:31:57,080
Dear Klao's soul…

429
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:00,120
It is in agony.

430
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,840
No one is coming to help.

431
00:32:09,440 --> 00:32:10,280
Young man.

432
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,960
What brings you to this place?

433
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:18,040
Did the forest lead you astray?

434
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:22,480
"Dear Klao's soul"?

435
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,280
So is Klao really dead?

436
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:48,360
You came out and ate at last,

437
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:50,600
you grumpy cat.

438
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:36,960
An earthquake!
The Great Fish has turned!

439
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:50,560
<i>Why are you getting emotional</i>
<i>in Klao's place again?</i>

440
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,360
Klao! Klao!

441
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:54,240
What is the trouble?

442
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:55,720
What brings these tears?

443
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:57,800
What has the Oracle done to you?

444
00:33:58,480 --> 00:34:00,080
What have you done to my brother?

445
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:02,640
I have yet to do anything.

446
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:08,280
What is all this commotion, Phop?
I can hear it from the front of the manor.

447
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:14,760
As if causing trouble in the capital
were not enough,

448
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:16,560
the Oracle followed us to our manor

449
00:34:16,639 --> 00:34:18,560
and brought him to tears.

450
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:22,960
No, I have done nothing.

451
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:26,880
Phop.

452
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:32,440
Take pity on her,
for she has gone mad, as Klao has.

453
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,560
I know you mean no harm.

454
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:41,719
Upon seeing him, you likely felt the urge
to offer a prophecy,

455
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:44,000
hoping to be of some help, right?

456
00:34:44,080 --> 00:34:45,400
Help…

457
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,840
Yes, I wish to help him.

458
00:34:49,040 --> 00:34:50,440
Here.

459
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:52,840
Consider this your payment.

460
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:56,320
It is time for you
to head back to your manor.

461
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:02,840
I am deeply grateful to you, my Lady.

462
00:35:14,200 --> 00:35:17,320
In some matters,
a calm approach is far more effective

463
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:20,320
than a loud outburst, Phop.

464
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:33,440
The Oracle is a pitiful soul.

465
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:37,800
She was cast out of the palace
merely for being different in nature.

466
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:43,160
She appears deranged now,
for she has been beaten senseless.

467
00:35:45,080 --> 00:35:46,520
Senselessly beaten…

468
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:50,920
Just like what they did to my father.

469
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,520
You are correct.

470
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:54,880
Before that cruel punishment,

471
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:56,640
her prophecies were without equal.

472
00:35:58,240 --> 00:36:01,040
A tragedy of fate and past karma,

473
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:04,240
that she should suffer
such cruel punishment and lose her mind.

474
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,880
Phop,

475
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,880
do not hold such bitterness against her.

476
00:36:10,160 --> 00:36:12,080
I hold nothing against her.

477
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:16,080
I am merely displeased
that she made him cry.

478
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:20,080
No, Phop.

479
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:24,720
I cried on my own.

480
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:34,920
My body aches so.
Age is finally catching up with me.

481
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:38,520
I have spent the better part of the day
with my friends.

482
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:40,720
Now, I shall retire to rest.

483
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:42,880
Be gentle with him, will you?

484
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:44,600
Understood.

485
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:47,560
Sai.

486
00:36:48,600 --> 00:36:50,320
Escort me.

487
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,720
-Say what you must--
-Go ahead and ask.

488
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:25,600
I guess we'll each take turns
asking questions.

489
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:27,680
You go first.

490
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:29,880
Certainly.

491
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:36,720
You told everyone
that you had lost your memory.

492
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:41,760
You have no recollection of me
or of anyone in this manor.

493
00:37:43,560 --> 00:37:44,920
And yet, that oracle…

494
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:47,680
You remember her perfectly well,

495
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:50,000
and you seemed
rather desperate to talk to her.

496
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:51,560
Why is it so?

497
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:54,240
Are you two acquainted?

498
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:59,120
Why don't you want me
to talk to her?

499
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:03,080
We agreed to exchange questions,

500
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:05,880
yet you have not answered mine.

501
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:11,080
I suggested we exchange questions,

502
00:38:11,160 --> 00:38:13,640
but I didn't say
we had to take turns answering them.

503
00:38:13,720 --> 00:38:15,160
Klao.

504
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:19,960
Well…

505
00:38:20,960 --> 00:38:23,160
When I was in Phichit,

506
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:27,040
I met someone

507
00:38:28,120 --> 00:38:29,760
who looked like her.

508
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:34,000
But I'm not sure whether

509
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:38,000
she was the same person I met.

510
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:44,160
You began to cry
as soon as you learned the truth?

511
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:52,960
It is your turn.
What is it that you wish to know?

512
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:57,560
You don't want me to talk to her
because she's weird?

513
00:38:58,600 --> 00:38:59,640
I mean, deranged.

514
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,000
And

515
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:04,800
the answer had better not be,

516
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:07,400
"I'm concerned about you."

517
00:39:11,360 --> 00:39:12,360
You there.

518
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:16,400
Tell Chuay to ready my vessel.

519
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:18,480
I intend to take him elsewhere.

520
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:19,880
Yes, my Lord.

521
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:24,400
Where to?

522
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:29,240
To seek the truth.

523
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:48,880
Where is Jom?

524
00:39:52,360 --> 00:39:53,520
Jom.

525
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:55,120
Jom…

526
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,680
I shall take these herbal remedies and…

527
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:19,160
Jom.

528
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:21,960
Why must you bathe
at this hour of all times?

529
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:36,960
I have been at work all day
and am covered in sweat.

530
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:38,640
Am I not to be permitted a bath?

531
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,360
And why are you hiding?

532
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:48,400
Come down and speak with me
if you have something to discuss.

533
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,000
It is nothing.

534
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,120
I came only to tell you
that I am returning.

535
00:40:55,320 --> 00:40:56,760
Take your time with your bath.

536
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:59,360
I shall wait for you upstairs.

537
00:41:01,560 --> 00:41:03,400
Come and wait for me at the pier now.

538
00:41:04,120 --> 00:41:05,960
What cause have you for embarrassment?

539
00:41:42,040 --> 00:41:43,440
Come closer.

540
00:41:57,880 --> 00:42:00,920
Have the herbal remedies been set
in their proper cabinet?

541
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:03,520
Yes, the fresh ones
are still laid out to dry.

542
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:06,760
The dried herbs are kept
in the leftmost cabinet within the manor.

543
00:42:07,640 --> 00:42:09,960
Look at me when you address me.

544
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:30,520
Are you shy with me?

545
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:34,600
We are both men.

546
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:36,360
What is there to be shy about…

547
00:42:39,360 --> 00:42:41,800
-apart from--
-No, I am not.

548
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,400
Very well.

549
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:47,680
Then look well upon me.

550
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:49,280
Jom.

551
00:42:59,080 --> 00:43:00,320
As I thought.

552
00:43:00,400 --> 00:43:03,320
You are thinking of something wicked,
are you not, Kaew?

553
00:43:09,720 --> 00:43:11,160
Jom.

554
00:43:13,640 --> 00:43:17,480
Do you despise me so greatly
that you would act thus?

555
00:43:19,800 --> 00:43:20,800
No.

556
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:24,080
I was but jesting with you,
as friends often do.

557
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:32,000
There is no need for you
to trouble yourself over the matter.

558
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:47,560
Why are we here?

559
00:44:50,360 --> 00:44:53,000
We used to play here
in our childhood days.

560
00:45:02,640 --> 00:45:04,160
Klao!

561
00:45:04,960 --> 00:45:06,680
Where might you be, Klao?

562
00:45:07,560 --> 00:45:09,080
Come out, will you not, Klao?

563
00:45:10,160 --> 00:45:13,360
Where are you?
Where are you hiding, Klao?

564
00:45:16,400 --> 00:45:17,400
Klao!

565
00:45:19,120 --> 00:45:21,080
Klao! Where are you?

566
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:28,040
Klao, wake up.

567
00:45:28,120 --> 00:45:29,200
Klao…

568
00:45:38,720 --> 00:45:42,200
You have lost.
You have failed to find me.

569
00:45:44,240 --> 00:45:47,680
Goodness, you were here all along,
hiding and sleeping

570
00:45:47,760 --> 00:45:49,600
without a sound.

571
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:51,680
How could you expect me to find
you at all?

572
00:45:51,760 --> 00:45:53,000
Do not blame me for this.

573
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:55,160
It was you who could not find me.

574
00:45:55,240 --> 00:45:57,880
Fine. I gave up.

575
00:45:58,600 --> 00:45:59,920
Come.

576
00:46:00,760 --> 00:46:02,480
The sun is about to set.

577
00:46:03,080 --> 00:46:04,000
Let us return.

578
00:46:12,800 --> 00:46:15,760
Phop… Phop! Take a look.

579
00:46:16,480 --> 00:46:19,440
What are those things
that fly so high in the sky?

580
00:46:19,520 --> 00:46:22,840
Oh, those are paper kites.

581
00:46:25,880 --> 00:46:29,440
One day, I shall tie myself to a kite

582
00:46:30,240 --> 00:46:32,160
and soar high in the sky.

583
00:46:32,240 --> 00:46:34,400
Help make it come true, will you?

584
00:46:35,520 --> 00:46:36,680
Of course.

585
00:46:50,400 --> 00:46:51,240
Phop.

586
00:46:53,880 --> 00:46:57,920
Where have you been taking him
until this hour of night?

587
00:46:58,000 --> 00:47:02,040
I only took him out
to play in the rice fields, Mother.

588
00:47:02,120 --> 00:47:05,040
I was the one
who insisted that he go out to play,

589
00:47:05,120 --> 00:47:06,760
and I accidentally fell asleep.

590
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:08,720
He bears no fault in this, aunt.

591
00:47:08,800 --> 00:47:11,560
Did you both
enjoy yourselves while playing?

592
00:47:11,640 --> 00:47:12,560
We did.

593
00:47:12,640 --> 00:47:14,320
-We did.
-We played hide and seek.

594
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:17,080
We also saw the farmers
flying paper kites.

595
00:47:18,040 --> 00:47:19,040
Good.

596
00:47:19,840 --> 00:47:21,400
You shared joy together,

597
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:24,920
so you must likewise
stand together through hardship.

598
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:59,040
Next time, let this be a reminder
to look out for each other

599
00:47:59,120 --> 00:48:01,080
and not lose track of time.

600
00:48:02,520 --> 00:48:03,760
-Understood.
-Yes, Mother.

601
00:48:09,960 --> 00:48:11,880
Each time Mother punished you,

602
00:48:12,440 --> 00:48:14,600
my heart ached for you.

603
00:48:14,680 --> 00:48:17,840
Could I take the blows in your stead,
I truly would.

604
00:48:22,880 --> 00:48:24,360
And yet,

605
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:27,280
we return here often…

606
00:48:29,640 --> 00:48:31,280
for the evening view

607
00:48:31,920 --> 00:48:33,920
is more beautiful than anywhere else.

608
00:48:36,360 --> 00:48:37,920
Now that we are grown,

609
00:48:38,800 --> 00:48:41,160
whenever your heart is troubled…

610
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:47,520
I know exactly where to find you.

611
00:48:56,280 --> 00:48:58,440
I had a feeling
I would find you hiding here.

612
00:49:01,320 --> 00:49:03,000
You already know, do you not?

613
00:49:05,520 --> 00:49:07,640
I must accompany Father to Phichit.

614
00:49:14,080 --> 00:49:15,800
I have no desire to depart with him.

615
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:19,000
The city feels far too distant from here.

616
00:49:20,880 --> 00:49:22,840
I do not wish to be parted from you.

617
00:49:30,400 --> 00:49:32,200
Who says it is too distant from here?

618
00:49:34,200 --> 00:49:35,640
Traveling by merchant ship,

619
00:49:35,720 --> 00:49:38,200
it should take me there
in no more than three weeks.

620
00:49:38,280 --> 00:49:40,120
Three full weeks.

621
00:49:42,200 --> 00:49:44,480
And you will be part of the city patrol.

622
00:49:46,360 --> 00:49:50,560
How can you expect to find the time
to come see me as far as Phichit?

623
00:49:53,960 --> 00:49:55,480
Stay in Phichit

624
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:57,960
and devote yourself to your education.

625
00:49:58,520 --> 00:50:01,840
Perhaps next year you could take the exam
and join the patrol with me?

626
00:50:04,680 --> 00:50:05,760
I would rather not.

627
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:08,320
I have never had any ambition.

628
00:50:09,280 --> 00:50:11,080
And what is it you wish to become?

629
00:50:14,560 --> 00:50:16,000
I do not exactly know.

630
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:21,120
I only know one thing.

631
00:50:24,360 --> 00:50:27,280
I am certain of my desire
to remain here with you.

632
00:50:28,360 --> 00:50:29,400
That is all.

633
00:50:38,960 --> 00:50:40,840
Every evening while you were gone,

634
00:50:41,600 --> 00:50:43,360
I came here to wait for you,

635
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:46,760
believing that you would one day return.

636
00:50:49,080 --> 00:50:51,720
And at last, I found you again.

637
00:51:00,080 --> 00:51:03,640
To watch the sun fade beyond the horizon
with you again

638
00:51:05,080 --> 00:51:07,720
is all I ever wished for in this world.

639
00:51:28,880 --> 00:51:31,880
If anything is weighing on your heart,
I am here to listen.

640
00:51:31,960 --> 00:51:34,120
I shall simply listen without judgment.

641
00:51:35,320 --> 00:51:37,520
I shall not judge
nor dictate your choices.

642
00:51:39,360 --> 00:51:42,200
And if you need my help,
I'm at your service.

643
00:51:57,480 --> 00:51:59,760
There is no rush,
should you not yet be ready.

644
00:52:00,840 --> 00:52:02,440
But remember this.

645
00:52:03,120 --> 00:52:05,360
I shall always be here,
standing by your side.

646
00:52:19,200 --> 00:52:20,480
Let us return.

647
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:23,240
Dusk draws near.

648
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:30,360
Please let me go.

649
00:53:30,440 --> 00:53:31,880
I'm fine now.

650
00:53:31,960 --> 00:53:33,360
No.

651
00:53:34,120 --> 00:53:36,440
I shall not let you slip
from my grasp again.

652
00:53:37,840 --> 00:53:39,880
I shall forever take care of you, my Klao.

653
00:54:13,040 --> 00:54:15,560
<i>What is this? What's happening?</i>

654
00:54:15,640 --> 00:54:17,200
<i>Why do I feel this way?</i>

655
00:54:17,280 --> 00:54:19,200
<i>I've never felt this way before.</i>

656
00:54:22,680 --> 00:54:23,680
Hands up!

657
00:54:23,760 --> 00:54:26,000
Hands ready? In three and four!

658
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:31,400
Thee, your posture is wrong.

659
00:54:36,800 --> 00:54:38,120
Make it stronger.

660
00:54:43,040 --> 00:54:44,880
Well done, Nakhun.

661
00:54:46,480 --> 00:54:48,080
What a lovely smile you've got.

662
00:54:49,280 --> 00:54:52,200
A little bit higher, okay?

663
00:54:52,280 --> 00:54:53,400
Okay.

664
00:54:56,640 --> 00:54:58,080
Nakhun.

665
00:54:58,160 --> 00:55:00,240
I think Nam Ngio is into you.

666
00:55:00,880 --> 00:55:02,400
What the hell are you on about?

667
00:55:02,480 --> 00:55:04,400
She only compliments you.

668
00:55:04,960 --> 00:55:07,960
You like her?
I can give you her contact details.

669
00:55:08,040 --> 00:55:12,040
I'm good. I can help your face
meet the ground. Want me to?

670
00:55:12,840 --> 00:55:14,480
Since junior high school,

671
00:55:15,240 --> 00:55:17,800
I've never seen you date anyone.

672
00:55:17,880 --> 00:55:19,880
Same goes for you.

673
00:55:19,960 --> 00:55:21,720
Yet the world didn't end, did it?

674
00:55:21,800 --> 00:55:26,400
Don't you ever get
that butterfly feeling in your stomach?

675
00:55:27,400 --> 00:55:30,040
No, all I feel in my stomach
is digestive juices.

676
00:55:30,120 --> 00:55:32,280
They're overflowing and not stopping.

677
00:55:33,920 --> 00:55:36,560
Haven't you ever felt excited
looking at someone?

678
00:55:38,200 --> 00:55:39,320
<i>Is this what it's like</i>

679
00:55:40,080 --> 00:55:43,680
<i>to have butterflies in my stomach?</i>

680
00:55:44,320 --> 00:55:46,760
<i>Have I actually gotten excited?</i>

681
00:55:47,800 --> 00:55:50,280
<i>I have a crush on…</i>

682
00:55:50,360 --> 00:55:52,200
<i>that deadpan-looking guy?</i>

683
00:55:52,880 --> 00:55:54,320
<i>I can't.</i>

684
00:55:54,400 --> 00:55:55,960
<i>Is this an obstacle</i>

685
00:55:56,680 --> 00:55:59,800
<i>stopping me from completing my mission?</i>

686
00:55:59,880 --> 00:56:02,680
I shall not let you slip away
from my grasp again.

687
00:56:04,080 --> 00:56:06,120
I shall forever take care of you, my Klao.

688
00:56:14,720 --> 00:56:16,680
<i>"My Klao…"</i>

689
00:56:23,120 --> 00:56:24,840
<i>It's not "my Nakhun," all right?</i>

690
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:35,520
You come at a perfect time.

691
00:56:43,760 --> 00:56:45,040
Klao.

692
00:56:45,480 --> 00:56:46,920
So you are already acquainted?

693
00:56:48,320 --> 00:56:51,120
He met Varna at the market only a day ago.

694
00:56:51,200 --> 00:56:53,320
Mm…

695
00:56:53,400 --> 00:56:55,080
This is High Lord Soontrapinit,

696
00:56:55,160 --> 00:56:57,640
father of Lord Harn,
whom you have met.

697
00:56:57,720 --> 00:56:59,640
He is also the uncle of Varna.

698
00:57:01,640 --> 00:57:03,480
Pray, give him your respects.

699
00:57:04,120 --> 00:57:07,920
Oh, is he Dear Klao,
the son of Lord Preechapiban?

700
00:57:08,960 --> 00:57:10,560
Oh, do join us.

701
00:57:17,760 --> 00:57:20,480
I have brought
a large collection of gifts from Lavo.

702
00:57:23,520 --> 00:57:26,320
Pray offer my thanks
to High Lord Dech Kraisor.

703
00:57:27,600 --> 00:57:30,680
But next time,
pray do not feel obliged to bring so much.

704
00:57:30,760 --> 00:57:34,600
I wouldn't want our sensitive cook
to be disheartened.

705
00:57:36,040 --> 00:57:36,920
Is that so?

706
00:57:41,560 --> 00:57:42,600
Certainly not.

707
00:57:42,680 --> 00:57:44,360
After all,

708
00:57:44,920 --> 00:57:48,960
we shall soon be family.

709
00:57:54,240 --> 00:57:56,440
Come, the feast awaits.

710
00:58:11,040 --> 00:58:12,640
<i>He's about to get married.</i>

711
00:58:13,200 --> 00:58:15,680
<i>Hold back your thoughts and feelings.</i>

712
00:58:18,720 --> 00:58:21,560
<i>Complete the mission and return home.</i>

713
00:58:22,200 --> 00:58:25,200
<i>You'd be better off quitting</i>
<i>the game before it starts, Nakhun!</i>

714
00:58:54,920 --> 00:58:56,520
Klao, come
and enjoy this with me.

715
00:58:58,400 --> 00:59:00,560
I should like to see
the swordplay of Phichit.

716
00:59:00,640 --> 00:59:01,720
Let me see your art.

717
00:59:06,520 --> 00:59:09,640
<i>This is the house of pleasure.</i>

718
00:59:09,720 --> 00:59:15,000
<i>What brings a gentleman such as yourself</i>
<i>to a place like this, Klao?</i>

719
00:59:15,080 --> 00:59:16,560
I can no longer wait.

720
00:59:16,640 --> 00:59:19,640
<i>By now, Phop must be terribly worried.</i>
